  "title": "Pasteur Rabies Vaccine",
  "summary": "In July 1885 Louis Pasteur and colleagues gave nine-year-old Joseph Meister, bitten by a rabid dog, a series of 14 daily doses of inactivated rabies virus from rabbit spinal cord. The boy survived, and the case is described as the start of the modern era of immunization.",
